        {
            "author_association": "MEMBER",
            "body": "Thanks for the PR!\r\n\r\nThis is a bit too much added configuration. This is already possible with available `MiniFilesWindowUpdate` `User` event. Like this:\r\n\r\n```lua\r\nlocal add_focused_linenumber = function(ev)\r\n  local win_id = ev.data.win_id\r\n  vim.wo[win_id].number = win_id == vim.api.nvim_get_current_win()\r\nend\r\nvim.api.nvim_create_autocmd('User', { pattern = 'MiniFilesWindowUpdate', callback = add_focused_linenumber })\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis approach is similar to the one described in [\"Customizing windows\"](https://nvim-mini.org/mini.nvim/doc/mini-files.html#minifiles-examples-customizewindows) example.\r\n\r\nClosing as not planned.",
