            "author_association": "NONE",
            "body": " \r\n> This is a bit too much added configuration. This is already possible with available `MiniFilesWindowUpdate` `User` event. Like this:\r\n\r\nHi! That approach results in the aforementioned one frame delay which can look really ugly... I understand the philosophy behind mini but I think this would be very fitting as it is very similar to a vim buffer\r\nI'm sure you've given this enough thought to provide a recipe, but I think its still probably valuable considering one of the people that replied uses it in their config. Thanks a lot",
